    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0342" n="272" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg272"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 183.9 Russia/5: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Archangel</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Archangel</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-16T18:00:00+03:31"
                            >December 16, 1918—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 17—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>37. For Colonel House.
                        Maklikoff<anchor n="3" xml:id="d299-f1"/> has
                    telegraphed Tchikowski<anchor n="4" xml:id="d299-f2"/> from
                    Paris saying that while the absence of a proper Russian Government excludes
                    Russia from official representation at the Peace Conference it is hoped to have
                    certain unofficial representatives and it would be well in
                        Maklikoff’s view if Tchikowski
                    were among these. The latter has replied that he will come if he can arrange to
                    commit his duties at Archangel to other hands. He hopes that General Meuller who
                    is now on the way here from Rome can replace him. He could then reach Paris
                    before the end of January.</p>
                <p>
                    Noulens<anchor n="5" xml:id="d299-f3"/> left here
                    yesterday.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Poole</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d299-f1" n="3" xml:id="d299-f1-content">
                <p>
                    V. A. Maklikoff, appointed by the Russian Provisional
                    Government as Ambassador to France.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d299-f2" n="4" xml:id="d299-f2-content">
                <p>
                    N. V. Tchikowski, President of the Russian Government of
                    the Northern Region.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d299-f3" n="5" xml:id="d299-f3-content">
                <p>
                    Joseph Noulens, French Ambassador to Russia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
